s10-7-p2 : Block
s10-7-p2 = prose (cons "A program may compute an executable representation, start it, record observations, replace part of its state, or change how its constituent computations interact. Dynamic software updating has an established technical literature ([40](#ref-40), [41](#ref-41)); the update below is a defined transition of the particular represented program. Such operations are themselves programs over the relevant machine and environment definitions. Their correctness is a predicate over the actual before-and-after executions. For example, if a particular application represents a live state by \(s:S\), an update by \(u:S\to S'\), and an invariant by \(I:S\to\mathcal U\), preservation is a term of type" nil)
